 34AR    32S(3HE,NG)                   1974GR19,1974BE18,1972CA22ENSDF    202609
 34AR  H TYP=FUL$AUT=LIJIE SUN AND JUN CHEN$CIT=ENSDF$CUT=30-Sep-2026$          
 34AR  H TYP=FUL$AUT=NINEL NICA, BALRAJ SINGH$CIT=NDS 113, 1563 (2012)$         
 34AR2 H CUT=28-May-2012$                                                       
 34AR c  1974Be18: an 8-MeV {+3}He beam was provided from the ANU EN tandem     
 34AR2c  accelerator and impinged on cooled sulphur targets. Neutrons were      
 34AR3c  detected using an NE213 liquid scintillator and |g rays were detected  
 34AR4c  using a Ge(Li) detector and a NaI(Tl) detector. Measured E|g, I|g,     
 34AR5c  n|g-coin, n|g(|q). Deduced levels, J, |g-ray branching ratios; deduced 
 34AR6c  lifetimes for 4 levels using DSAM.                                     
 34AR c  1974Gr19: 8-12-MeV {+3}He beams were provided from the 7-MV Van de     
 34AR2c  Graaff accelerator at the University of Freiburg and impinged on       
 34AR3c  natural ZnS targets. Neutrons were detected using an annular NE213     
 34AR4c  liquid scintillator and |g rays were detected using a Ge(Li) detector  
 34AR5c  and 5 NaI(Tl) detectors. Measured E|g, I|g, n|g-coin, and n|g|g-coin.  
 34AR6c  Deduced 10 levels, J, |g-ray branching ratios, and mixing ratios;      
 34AR7c  deduced lifetimes for 5 levels using DSAM.                             
 34AR c  1972Ca22: an 8.5-MeV {+3}He beam was provided from the Oxford          
 34AR2c  University tandem Van de Graaff generator and impinged on Ag{-2}S      
 34AR3c  targets. Neutrons were detected using a NE102 liquid scintillator. The 
 34AR4c  |g rays were detected using a Ge(Li) detector. Measured E|g, I|g,      
 34AR5c  E{-n}, I{-n}, and n|g(|q). Deduced lifetimes for 3 levels using DSAM.  
